  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nThe Freeze Warning is in effect until 9am this morning. With \noptimal radiational cooling taking place along with calm \nsurface flow and clear skies temperatures are progressively \ndropping to around freezing already in the northeast mountains \nand soon the rest of the area should follow. Most places should\nsee freezing or below which should end the growing season for \nus which would end issuing future products for frost/freeze. \nHowever, after collaboration will neighboring offices, the day \nshift will have to reassess which areas to be taken out of the \ngrowing season after this morning. This will allow for further \nguidance whether any future headlines are warranted here on out \nfor Monday and Tuesday mornings as temperatures will trend \ncooler than normal. By midweek, temperatures will moderate back \nto around seasonable for this time of year. Dry weather will \ncontinue as strong high pressure holds true for the region. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA strong omega type blocking pattern takes hold starting the new\nwork week and lasts through the weekend. This will bring mainly\nclear skies, lots of sunshine and moderating temperatures for \nthe rest of the work week and for next weekend. Medium range \nmodels do not have any precipitation in sight for the forecast. \nBesides some freeze or frost the next few mornings, the only \nother hazard will be the potential for dense valley fog each \nmorning through the short and long term periods of the forecast.",
